1:KLEE 3.3, 15 October 2026
2-=========================
3-
4-Incorporating changes from 24 December 2025 to 15 October 2026.
5-Maintainers during this time span: @ccadar
6:Documentation at https://klee-se.org/releases/docs/v3.3
7-
8-== Major features and important changes ==
9-- New KLEE Web version (@FinnLeh, @YiLai-qed)
10-- Execute unsupported intrinsics via external calls (@operasfantom)
11-
12:== LLVM support ==
13:- Current recommended version is LLVM 18
14:- Added full support for LLVM 17-19 (@ccadar)
15:- Removed support for LLVM < 15 (@ccadar)
16:- KLEE 3.3 will be the last version with support for LLVM 15
17-
18-== Options, scripts and KLEE intrinsics added, changed or removed ==
19-- Initialised the struct stats of symbolic files (A, B, ...) to fixed sane defaults. In particular, symbolic files are now regular files for which we have 
read and write permissions (@ccadar)
20-- Added support for the llvm.load.relative intrinsic (@ccadar)
21-- Added support for the llvm.ptrmask intrinsic (@ccadar)
22-- Improved support for the llvm.load.relative intrinsic (@ccadar)
23-
24-== Other changes ==
25:- Add support for the new pass manager of LLVM 17+ (@ccadar)
26:- Add UBSan support for the (LLVM 17+) function type mismatch handler ABI (@operasfantom)
27-- Enforced fd access mode checks for sym-file read/write operations (@dino-fan777)
28-- Moved FreeBSD CI from Cirrus CI to GitHub Actions (@arrowd)
29-- Fix a crash when runFunctionAsMain() is invoked multiple times, particularly when replaying multiple .ktest files (@nokitoino)
30-- Recompute GEP indices instead of accumulating them across runs (@nokitoino)
31-- Fixed permission checks in the POSIX runtime (@ccadar)
32-- Fixed dangling pointer in utimes() for symbolic files when the second argument is NULL (@fkil)
33-- Improvements to KLEE's freestanding library (@ccadar)
34-- Fixed issue with leaking solver shared memory segments (@ccadar)
35-- Added a UBSan tutorial (@5467845)
36-- Smaller refactorings, fixes and improvements, test cases, maintenance, comments, web version, website, etc. (@12300001111, @251, @arrowd, @ccadar, 
@danielschemmel, @davidtr1037, @dependabot, @foxtran, @jbuening, @operasfantom)
37-
38-
