40-==========================
41-
42-Incorporating changes from 1 March 2024 to 23 December 2025.
43-Maintainers during this time span: @ccadar, @MartinNowack, @251, @danielschemmel
44-Documentation at https://klee-se.org/releases/docs/v3.2
45-
46-== Major features and important changes ==
47-- KLEE acquired a new domain name: klee-se.org
48-- Added an option to generate XML test cases (@misonijnik)
49-- Improved the freestanding runtime (@mrexodia)
50-- Fixed support for concrete objects > 2^32 bytes (@ccadar)
51-
52:== LLVM support ==
53:- Current recommended version is LLVM 16
54:- Added partial support for LLVM 17-19 (@mrexodia)
55:- Removed support for LLVM < 13 (@ccadar)
56:- KLEE 3.2 will be the last version with support for LLVM <15
57-
58-== Options, scripts and KLEE intrinsics added, changed or removed ==
59-- Renamed --ignore-solver-failures to --ignore-stp-failures (@ccadar)
60-
61-== Other changes ==
62-- Added functions for comparing versions to build scripts (@ccadar)
63-- Added handler for _Exit (@fwc)
64-- Reorganised tests: (@ccadar)
65-- Disallow symbolic objects > 2^32 bytes, which were previously handled incorrectly (@ccadar)
66-- Smaller refactorings, fixes and improvements, test cases, maintenance, comments, web version, website, etc. (@251, @ccadar, @danielschemmel, @dependabot, 
@homyhost, @jamacku, @jbuening, @MartinNowack, @ricardaxel, @sp1ff, @sreeshmaheshwar, @xokdvium)
